    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC successfully triggered the heap double-free vulnerability. The ASAN output confirms the exact crash path:\n\n1. `buf` allocated at `flb_http_client.c:628`\n2. First free at `flb_http_client.c:720` via `flb_free(buf)`\n3. Second free (double-free) at `flb_http_client.c:1277` via `flb_http_client_destroy` → `flb_free(c->header_buf)`\n\nThe 120-byte input works by having an odd first byte (0x01) to enter the proxy branch, with content that doesn't match \"http://\" or \"https://\", causing `proxy_parse` to fail and triggering the double-free in the error-handling path.",
